                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-40347",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "python-multipart: Python-Multipart: Denial of Service via crafted multipart/form-data requests"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Python-Multipart is a streaming multipart parser for Python. Versions prior to 0.0.26 have a denial of service vulnerability when parsing crafted `multipart/form-data` requests with large preamble or epilogue sections. Upgrade to version 0.0.26 or later, which skips ahead to the next boundary candidate when processing leading CR/LF data and immediately discards epilogue data after the closing boundary."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "http./05-ai-llm-lab",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-40347\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: python-multipart\nFixed Version: 0.0.26\nLink: [CVE-2026-40347](http./05-ai-llm-lab is a streaming multipart parser for Python. Versions prior to 0.0.26 have a denial of service vulnerability when parsing crafted `multipart/form-data` requests with large preamble or epilogue sections. Upgrade to version 0.0.26 or later, which skips ahead to the next boundary candidate when processing leading CR/LF data and immediately discards epilogue data after the closing boundary.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-40347**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|python-multipart|0.0.26|[CVE-2026-40347](http./05-ai-llm-lab is a streaming multipart parser for Python. Versions prior to 0.0.26 have a denial of service vulnerability when parsing crafted `multipart/form-data` requests with large preamble or epilogue sections. Upgrade to version 0.0.26 or later, which skips ahead to the next boundary candidate when processing leading CR/LF data and immediately discards epilogue data after the closing boundary."
              },
              "properties": {
